{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"broke-choleric-hound","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Summary\n\nFound by the Step 7 (Axis 1 construct) sibling sweep while fixing `satiated-activated-aardwolf` (5524-e353-2e2d-4dbe). Same broad drift class — a source that affects the running environment is absent from every autodeploy path manifest — but a **different surface and disposition**, so it is filed rather than folded into the detect-only 5524 fix.\n\n`infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` is the MCP container ENTRYPOINT: `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` does `COPY . /app` then `RUN install -m 0755 /app/infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh /usr/local/bin/mcp-entrypoint.sh` and `ENTRYPOINT [\"/usr/local/bin/mcp-entrypoint.sh\"]`. It is baked into the image at build time.\n\n`autodeploy.sh`'s `MCP_PATHS='src/rebar infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp infra/compose/docker-compose.yml uv.lock pyproject.toml'` does **not** include `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh`, and it is in no other manifest. So a merged change to ONLY `mcp-entrypoint.sh` triggers no MCP rebuild — the running container keeps the stale entrypoint. Unlike the host-nginx materializers (5524, detect-only because applying means `nginx -s reload`), applying THIS is an ordinary MCP image rebuild, which is already inside the mcp target's v1 auto-apply scope.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:91,147,150` — `COPY . /app`; installs `mcp-entrypoint.sh` to `/usr/local/bin`; sets it as `ENTRYPOINT`.\n- `grep -oE \"^[A-Z_]+_PATHS='[^']*'\" infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh | grep mcp-entrypoint` → no match (absent from every manifest).\n\n## Suggested disposition (apply-parity, NOT detect-only)\n\nAdd `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` to `MCP_PATHS` so an entrypoint-source change rebuilds the MCP image via the existing blue-green mcp deploy path (this is apply, not signal — distinct from the ADR 0079 v1→v2 host-nginx reload boundary that kept 5524 detect-only). Add regression coverage mirroring `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_nginx_materializer.py` / the mcp-delta tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` is enumerated in `MCP_PATHS` (or otherwise triggers an MCP rebuild) so an entrypoint-source change is applied, not silently dropped.\n- [ ] Regression test drives `autodeploy.sh` under a git shim where only `mcp-entrypoint.sh` changed and asserts the MCP deploy path fires.","id":"5d4c-a25b-b612-4aca","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Autodeploy never rebuilds the MCP image on an mcp-entrypoint.sh source change — baked into the image but absent from MCP_PATHS (silent-drift sibling of 5524)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788116382515146845,"uuid":"983efa88-404d-4e68-b45a-10c3edf4a970"}